@javanna the current state is non-functional, but I [pushed](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/101373/commits/873a34f04c0f0a98d37e9d4db445f17a6a428deb) so you can see what I have done so far.
I'd be happy for advice on how I can debug the fetch phase and specifically the invocation of [`valueFetcher()`](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/b56e6e1f15cf14430d6e4a286e8619dc66670a21/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/IgnoredFieldMapper.java#L59). I didn't find a unit test that invokes it yet...

What I know is that the [`FetchDocValuesContext` that comes from the `FetchContext`](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/b56e6e1f15cf14430d6e4a286e8619dc66670a21/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/fetch/subphase/FetchDocValuesPhase.java#L33) is `null` and that [the doc values list that comes from the `SearchSourceBuilder`](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/b56e6e1f15cf14430d6e4a286e8619dc66670a21/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/SearchService.java#L1340) is also `null`. Not sure if this is any help...

